{title: Jesus Bids Us Shine}
{artist: Susan Warner / Edwin O. Excell}
{genre: Children}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Closing}
{key: G}
{tempo: 155}
{time: 4/4}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Cyber Hymnal score (Trinity Hymnal (Philadelphia, Pennsylvania: Orthodox Presbyterian Church, 1961), # 653)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Jesus bids us shine with a pure,__[D7]__ clear light,
[D7]Like a little candle [Am]burn[G]ing in the night.
[G]In this world of darkness [C]so let us [G7]shine—
[G7]You in your small corner, [C]and [G]I__[D7]__ in [G]mine.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]Jesus bids us shine, first of all__[D7]__ for Him;
[D7]Well He sees and knows it, [Am]if [G]our light grows dim.
[G]He looks down from Heaven [C]to see us [G7]shine—
[G7]You in your small corner, [C]and [G]I__[D7]__ in [G]mine.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]Jesus bids us shine, then, for all__[D7]__ around;
[D7]Many kinds of darkness [Am]in [G]the world are found—
[G]Sin and want and sorrow; [C]so we must [G7]shine—
[G7]You in your small corner, [C]and [G]I__[D7]__ in [G]mine.
{end_of_verse}
